SUMMARY:Rose City Self Defense Workshop
DESCRIPTION:The NEW Youth Introductory Class is 3 sessions\, each 2 hours in length. This Empowerment Self-Defense (ESD) class is designed to introduce youth to a variety of self-protective options in a discussion format.  Our student-centered training is designed to help youth identify their risks\, evaluate their strengths\, and explore their options for dealing with the threat of violence.  Topics Include:  Trusting and using your intuition; How bias affects your judgment; Establishing and setting boundaries; Assertive communication; The benefits and risks of various escape options; Healthy Relationships and consent; Physical Self-Defense Strikes and Escapes.  Youth Classes are open to youth ages 11 through 14.  Youth may attend alone or be accompanied by a women-identifying\, non-binary person comfortable in a space that centers on the experiences of girls or LGBTQIA2S+ adult. Snacks provided for all attendees. \nEditor’s note: This event is a community submission.
URL:https://pdxparent.com/event-single/rose-city-self-defense-workshop/2026-04-20/
LOCATION:Sellwood Community House\, 1436 SE Spokane St\, Portland\, Oregon\, 97202
CATEGORIES:Active,Educational,Kids Calendar,LGBTQ+
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://pdxparent.com/wp-content/uploads/Self-Defense-02-scaled.png
ORGANIZER;CN="Rose City Self Defense":MAILTO:himackenziegray@gmail.com
GEO:45.4647759;-122.6512239
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Sellwood Community House 1436 SE Spokane St Portland Oregon 97202;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=1436 SE Spokane St:geo:-122.6512239,45.4647759
END:VEVENT
